  "updatedRuleStatements": {
    "TS-04": "All 400, 401, and 403 responses must return a standardized JSON envelope containing error code, message, and requestId to ensure consistent API security compliance. Return exact nested JSON body { error: { code: 'ERR_...', message: '...', requestId: req.requestId } } on EVERY 400, 401, and 403 response (never return a flat string { error: '...' }).",
    "TS-10": "Validate that amountCents is an integer where amountCents > 0 and amountCents <= 10000000; reject invalid financial payouts with HTTP 400. Pair payout routes with: uppercase const ALLOWED_ROLES = [...]; if (!ALLOWED_ROLES.includes(ctx.session.role)) return 403; explicit if (ctx.session.tenantId !== payload.tenantId) return 403; exact nested error body { error: { code, message, requestId: req.requestId } } on all 4xx; and headers { 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' } on all responses.",
    "TS-11": "Multi-tenant admin export endpoints must project only non-sensitive exportFields and enforce a limit <= 500, returning 400 for any unbounded requests. Pair export routes with: uppercase const ALLOWED_ROLES = [...]; if (!ALLOWED_ROLES.includes(ctx.session.role)) return 403; explicit if (ctx.session.tenantId !== payload.tenantId) return 403; exact nested error body { error: { code, message, requestId: req.requestId } } on all 4xx; headers { 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' } on all responses; and ctx.emitAuditEvent({ action, actorId: ctx.session.userId, requestId: req.requestId }) on success."
  },
